[{:db/id "3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" :answer/id #uuid "3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} + \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,- 3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e687c503-1567-58df-be9a-1878259734e8" :answer/id #uuid "e687c503-1567-58df-be9a-1878259734e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} + \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a2a95bff-92b9-53c6-8fe5-0f0d43b2da54" :answer/id #uuid "a2a95bff-92b9-53c6-8fe5-0f0d43b2da54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,u \\cos{(v )},\\,\\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2d0c0d85-2f02-55dc-9473-202a33fde613" :answer/id #uuid "2d0c0d85-2f02-55dc-9473-202a33fde613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,\\sin{(v )},\\,- v \\sin{(u )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d47bf98b-95ef-5c6e-a01e-21e1f47b6e49" :answer/id #uuid "d47bf98b-95ef-5c6e-a01e-21e1f47b6e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} - \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,- 3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f47863d9-76b7-508b-9a8f-b6a3c48353d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "f47863d9-76b7-508b-9a8f-b6a3c48353d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" "e687c503-1567-58df-be9a-1878259734e8" "a2a95bff-92b9-53c6-8fe5-0f0d43b2da54" "2d0c0d85-2f02-55dc-9473-202a33fde613" "d47bf98b-95ef-5c6e-a01e-21e1f47b6e49"] :answer-field/correct "3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "5f82fba6-89f1-5c94-8cc8-c031a913d71e" :question/id #uuid "5f82fba6-89f1-5c94-8cc8-c031a913d71e" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨3\\left(u\\right),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(1\\right) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(1\\right) & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(1\\right) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,- 3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["f47863d9-76b7-508b-9a8f-b6a3c48353d0"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "f6825be3-48b8-58cc-a7e1-1b5a5360a776" :answer/id #uuid "f6825be3-48b8-58cc-a7e1-1b5a5360a776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" :answer/id #uuid "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e542ea0c-15b0-5e7c-bebb-9196a291740b" :answer/id #uuid "e542ea0c-15b0-5e7c-bebb-9196a291740b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨72 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,- 18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5ae97bc8-ceab-539c-b279-77e85c4ec979" :answer/id #uuid "5ae97bc8-ceab-539c-b279-77e85c4ec979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "707eea66-3c70-52f8-96ff-83c9270232ab" :answer/id #uuid "707eea66-3c70-52f8-96ff-83c9270232ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "17726b3e-da12-5100-9529-30dd30f97ab5" :answer-field/id #uuid "17726b3e-da12-5100-9529-30dd30f97ab5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f6825be3-48b8-58cc-a7e1-1b5a5360a776" "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" "e542ea0c-15b0-5e7c-bebb-9196a291740b" "5ae97bc8-ceab-539c-b279-77e85c4ec979" "707eea66-3c70-52f8-96ff-83c9270232ab"] :answer-field/correct "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "1f7b80e6-fd6c-56fc-be8d-0adb41e9046a" :question/id #uuid "1f7b80e6-fd6c-56fc-be8d-0adb41e9046a" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+1,\\,y=3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=4\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,4\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["17726b3e-da12-5100-9529-30dd30f97ab5"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d62667d1-734a-5e83-a94c-519d0e08464a" :answer/id #uuid "d62667d1-734a-5e83-a94c-519d0e08464a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,- 4 e^{v},\\,3⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e8db9f02-5e58-5d77-9a53-681489b491a2" :answer/id #uuid "e8db9f02-5e58-5d77-9a53-681489b491a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" :answer/id #uuid "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,4 e^{v},\\,3⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2175fd76-0c56-57b8-9174-0002272778f6" :answer/id #uuid "2175fd76-0c56-57b8-9174-0002272778f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bef9218d-e0fe-5ce0-82f9-bf47cfd7d97b" :answer/id #uuid "bef9218d-e0fe-5ce0-82f9-bf47cfd7d97b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12,\\,- 4 e^{v},\\,-3⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4775f4af-3673-54e1-9229-30258922e843" :answer-field/id #uuid "4775f4af-3673-54e1-9229-30258922e843" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d62667d1-734a-5e83-a94c-519d0e08464a" "e8db9f02-5e58-5d77-9a53-681489b491a2" "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" "2175fd76-0c56-57b8-9174-0002272778f6" "bef9218d-e0fe-5ce0-82f9-bf47cfd7d97b"] :answer-field/correct "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c43bafbb-27d1-589d-9395-34d1fb53b842" :question/id #uuid "c43bafbb-27d1-589d-9395-34d1fb53b842" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=3\\left(v\\right),\\,z=4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,3\\left(v\\right),\\,4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,4 e^{v},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["4775f4af-3673-54e1-9229-30258922e843"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "cf34330c-97e2-5157-b920-b9f0ebafbfa9" :answer/id #uuid "cf34330c-97e2-5157-b920-b9f0ebafbfa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b7590c8f-53c2-5e60-abe5-94dba4b54823" :answer/id #uuid "b7590c8f-53c2-5e60-abe5-94dba4b54823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,6 v^{2},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8d182813-aebd-50d7-b3b8-2aae19e921af" :answer/id #uuid "8d182813-aebd-50d7-b3b8-2aae19e921af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,- 48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "893aedc5-d336-51fd-a323-6bc046fac648" :answer/id #uuid "893aedc5-d336-51fd-a323-6bc046fac648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,2⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" :answer/id #uuid "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8a9644d7-6a0d-58f4-8f95-fffe69d2cb42" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9644d7-6a0d-58f4-8f95-fffe69d2cb42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["cf34330c-97e2-5157-b920-b9f0ebafbfa9" "b7590c8f-53c2-5e60-abe5-94dba4b54823" "8d182813-aebd-50d7-b3b8-2aae19e921af" "893aedc5-d336-51fd-a323-6bc046fac648" "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969"] :answer-field/correct "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f5c049c6-8f99-5422-a42e-c9b464f4ec2b" :question/id #uuid "f5c049c6-8f99-5422-a42e-c9b464f4ec2b" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=2u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6 v^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["8a9644d7-6a0d-58f4-8f95-fffe69d2cb42"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "f26aabe8-b114-5c96-bf02-8440e5209761" :answer/id #uuid "f26aabe8-b114-5c96-bf02-8440e5209761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 3 u \\cos{(u )} + 6 v^{2},\\,2 u - 2 v,\\,- 12 v + 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" :answer/id #uuid "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,- 2 u + 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "00e322d8-ea35-5e03-9ba3-b9169197298c" :answer/id #uuid "00e322d8-ea35-5e03-9ba3-b9169197298c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,6 v,\\,u⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5d22a2bd-bcc3-592e-a7f6-40f9aab6f703" :answer/id #uuid "5d22a2bd-bcc3-592e-a7f6-40f9aab6f703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,2 u - 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7a398103-fe6d-5bb1-982f-5e9709d919e7" :answer/id #uuid "7a398103-fe6d-5bb1-982f-5e9709d919e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,v⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "46102bec-425d-5814-92d4-891a6a84571f" :answer-field/id #uuid "46102bec-425d-5814-92d4-891a6a84571f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f26aabe8-b114-5c96-bf02-8440e5209761" "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" "00e322d8-ea35-5e03-9ba3-b9169197298c" "5d22a2bd-bcc3-592e-a7f6-40f9aab6f703" "7a398103-fe6d-5bb1-982f-5e9709d919e7"] :answer-field/correct "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2f1ae609-38a0-53f0-baa0-900f6821dc85" :question/id #uuid "2f1ae609-38a0-53f0-baa0-900f6821dc85" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = 2\\left(u + v\\right), y = 3\\left(v^{2} + \\sin u\\right), z = uv$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + 2 v,\\,3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )},\\,u v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u + 2 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u + 2 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,6 v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 \\cos{(u )} & v \\\\ 2 & 6 v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\cos{(u )} & v \\\\ 6 v & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & v \\\\ 2 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\cos{(u )} \\\\ 2 & 6 v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3 \\cos{(u )})(u)-(v)(6 v),\\,-[(2)(u)-(v)(2)],\\,(2)(6 v)-(3 \\cos{(u )})(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,- 2 u + 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["46102bec-425d-5814-92d4-891a6a84571f"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8957384e-fa9c-5800-9b29-602d86892550" :answer/id #uuid "8957384e-fa9c-5800-9b29-602d86892550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d022c4c7-0c21-5bf5-99c0-d849f94827ce" :answer/id #uuid "d022c4c7-0c21-5bf5-99c0-d849f94827ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3 v^{2},\\,2⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bc6fc1db-b13a-5b17-a1ee-f3152ebb05c0" :answer/id #uuid "bc6fc1db-b13a-5b17-a1ee-f3152ebb05c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" :answer/id #uuid "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "328d5447-3347-5040-9526-4d0f97f066b7" :answer/id #uuid "328d5447-3347-5040-9526-4d0f97f066b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,- 18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cb049baa-bb14-5762-b5a8-0e6bb3e655ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb049baa-bb14-5762-b5a8-0e6bb3e655ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8957384e-fa9c-5800-9b29-602d86892550" "d022c4c7-0c21-5bf5-99c0-d849f94827ce" "bc6fc1db-b13a-5b17-a1ee-f3152ebb05c0" "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" "328d5447-3347-5040-9526-4d0f97f066b7"] :answer-field/correct "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "e182b79a-69d6-51fa-bb1c-78fc47b34b3a" :question/id #uuid "e182b79a-69d6-51fa-bb1c-78fc47b34b3a" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y={v}^{3}+1,\\,z=2\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["cb049baa-bb14-5762-b5a8-0e6bb3e655ce"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d39e64d9-d1b0-54f3-8894-9323b7b1df99" :answer/id #uuid "d39e64d9-d1b0-54f3-8894-9323b7b1df99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" :answer/id #uuid "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "517f96df-2944-53eb-b50d-17f1387e43ea" :answer/id #uuid "517f96df-2944-53eb-b50d-17f1387e43ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨72 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,- 36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6685d10d-ae48-537c-b0e4-0a386d10674a" :answer/id #uuid "6685d10d-ae48-537c-b0e4-0a386d10674a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "64e9e700-d3cd-54f5-b9b2-d40f9cb5c9d8" :answer/id #uuid "64e9e700-d3cd-54f5-b9b2-d40f9cb5c9d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dc616a45-3e00-5d64-b7a9-e4fced4e40f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc616a45-3e00-5d64-b7a9-e4fced4e40f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d39e64d9-d1b0-54f3-8894-9323b7b1df99" "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" "517f96df-2944-53eb-b50d-17f1387e43ea" "6685d10d-ae48-537c-b0e4-0a386d10674a" "64e9e700-d3cd-54f5-b9b2-d40f9cb5c9d8"] :answer-field/correct "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "afa8c161-9dec-5962-a3c6-b42a56e57915" :question/id #uuid "afa8c161-9dec-5962-a3c6-b42a56e57915" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=4\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,4\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(2u\\right) & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["dc616a45-3e00-5d64-b7a9-e4fced4e40f6"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "e811bfc6-8c6f-5dc9-955e-158552f9c970" :answer/id #uuid "e811bfc6-8c6f-5dc9-955e-158552f9c970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1